Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH 1/2] Link the current gtest CMake targets

Link the current gtest CMake targets

GoogleTest 1.13 renamed its exported CMake targets from GTest::GTest /
GTest::Main to GTest::gtest / GTest::gtest_main, and 1.14 removed the old
names. mtxclient 0.10.1 (released 2025-08) still links the old ones, so with
the packaged gtest 1.17.0 configuration fails with

    Target "client_api" links to:
      GTest::GTest
    but the target was not found.

gtest-config.cmake, which CMakeDeps generates for the packaged gtest, exports
GTest::gtest and GTest::gtest_main; the gtest package also installs its own
GTestConfig.cmake with the same two names. Switching the fifteen test targets
to the current names therefore works both through the Conan package and against
a system-wide gtest >= 1.13.

A pkg-config route was evaluated first and rejected: the packaged gtest recipe
declares cpp_info.libs = ["gtest"] only, so PkgConfigDeps emits gtest.pc and no
gtest_main.pc -- pkg_check_modules(gtest_main ...) cannot resolve here.

Only the test executables inside if(BUILD_LIB_TESTS) change; the library target
is untouched.
Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony PC adaptation <noreply@example.com>
